      "returncode": 0,
      "stdout": "usage: ascend_server.py [-h] --checkpoint CHECKPOINT --hixl-host HIXL_HOST\n                        [--hixl-port-base HIXL_PORT_BASE]\n                        [--hixl-library HIXL_LIBRARY] [--bind-host BIND_HOST]\n                        [--ctrl-port CTRL_PORT] [--http-port HTTP_PORT]\n                        [--capacity CAPACITY] [--mtp-width {1,2,4}]\n                        [--expert-bank] --output OUTPUT\n\nServe batch-one greedy GLM-5.2 decode on one sixteen-die A3 host.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --checkpoint CHECKPOINT\n  --hixl-host HIXL_HOST\n                        numeric business IP advertised by HIXL\n  --hixl-port-base HIXL_PORT_BASE\n  --hixl-library HIXL_LIBRARY\n  --bind-host BIND_HOST\n  --ctrl-port CTRL_PORT\n  --http-port HTTP_PORT\n  --capacity CAPACITY\n  --mtp-width {1,2,4}   1: serial decode; 2/4: greedy MTP verification\n  --expert-bank\n  --output OUTPUT\n",
      "stderr": ""
    },
    {
      "command": [
        "/root/miniconda3/bin/python3",
        "tests/glm52/run_native_mtp_session.py",
        "--help"
      ],
      "returncode": 0,
      "stdout": "usage: run_native_mtp_session.py [-h] --checkpoint CHECKPOINT\n                                 --tokens TOKENS [TOKENS ...]\n                                 [--prefix PREFIX] [--mtp-prefix MTP_PREFIX]\n                                 [--width {2,4}] [--max-tokens MAX_TOKENS]\n                                 [--capacity CAPACITY] [--expert-bank]\n                                 --output OUTPUT --source-commit SOURCE_COMMIT\n\nCompare the TP16 serving loop with serial CANN AR and MTP caches. Use a cold\nprompt or paired main/MTP prefixes as in run_native_mtp_rounds. Requests run\nnormally, cancel before delivery, cancel after one/two tokens, then repeat\nnormally. This checks CANN execution consistency, not HF parity or HIXL\ntransfer. The production serving factory and TP command loop run.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --checkpoint CHECKPOINT\n  --tokens TOKENS [TOKENS ...]\n  --prefix PREFIX\n  --mtp-prefix MTP_PREFIX\n  --width {2,4}\n  --max-tokens MAX_TOKENS\n  --capacity CAPACITY\n  --expert-bank\n  --output OUTPUT\n  --source-commit SOURCE_COMMIT\n",
      "stderr": ""
    },
    {
      "command": [
        "/root/miniconda3/bin/python3",
        "tests/glm52/run_native_mtp_rounds.py",
        "--help"
      ],
      "returncode": 0,
      "stdout": "usage: run_native_mtp_rounds.py [-h] --checkpoint CHECKPOINT\n                                --tokens TOKENS [TOKENS ...] [--prefix PREFIX]\n                                [--mtp-prefix MTP_PREFIX] [--width {2,4}]\n                                [--max-tokens MAX_TOKENS]\n                                [--capacity CAPACITY] [--expert-bank]\n                                --output OUTPUT --source-commit SOURCE_COMMIT\n\nCompare speculative CANN rounds with serial AR and MTP teacher forcing. This\nis an execution-consistency check, not independent HF numerical parity. The\noptional main prefix is the usual 78-layer rank-N.pt bundle. The MTP prefix\nbundle has metadata_sha256 and layer (latent/rope/index_keys). With prefixes,\n--tokens contains only the last prompt token; it is replayed at P-1 to recover\nthe normalized parent and first generated token.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --checkpoint CHECKPOINT\n  --tokens TOKENS [TOKENS ...]\n  --prefix PREFIX\n  --mtp-prefix MTP_PREFIX\n  --width {2,4}\n  --max-tokens MAX_TOKENS\n  --capacity CAPACITY\n  --expert-bank\n  --output OUTPUT\n  --source-commit SOURCE_COMMIT\n",
